#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:336
msgid "Conducting a mesh refinement study"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:338
msgid ""
"In order to investigate the influence of the mesh on the solution we must "
"solve the model multiple times, increasing the mesh resolution as we go. We "
"first create a list of the number of points per domain we would like to use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:-1
msgid "[7]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:-1
msgid "npts = [4, 8, 16, 32, 64]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:359
msgid ""
"and now we can loop over the list, creating and solving simulations as we "
"go. The solutions are stored in the list ``solutions``, similar to what we "
"did in `Tutorial 2 <./tutorial-2-compare-models.ipynb>`__ for the various "
"models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:-1
msgid "[8]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:-1
msgid ""
"# choose model and parameters\n"
"model = pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN()\n"
"parameter_values = pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Ecker2015\")\n"
"\n"
"# loop over number of mesh points\n"
"solutions = []\n"
"for N in npts:\n"
"    var_pts = {\n"
"        \"x_n\": N,  # negative electrode\n"
"        \"x_s\": N,  # separator\n"
"        \"x_p\": N,  # positive electrode\n"
"        \"r_n\": N,  # negative particle\n"
"        \"r_p\": N,  # positive particle\n"
"    }\n"
"    sim = pybamm.Simulation(model, parameter_values=parameter_values, "
"var_pts=var_pts)\n"
"    sim.solve([0, 3600])\n"
"    solutions.append(sim.solution)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:396
msgid ""
"We can now pass our list of solutions to the dynamic plot method, allowing "
"use to see the influence of the mesh on the computed voltage. We pass our "
"list of points using the ``labels`` keyword so that the plots are labeled "
"with the number of points used in the simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:-1
msgid "[9]:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/getting_started/tutorial-9-changing-the-mesh.ipynb:-1
msgid "pybamm.dynamic_plot(solutions, [\"Voltage [V]\"], labels=npts)"
msgstr ""

